      "why_read": "This text explains why current agent skill integration leads to reliability issues due to scarce model attention. Readers will learn about a new skill protocol designed to mitigate these problems by optimizing prompt space.",
      "authors": [
        "Dr. Atlas Wang"
      ],
      "content": "Agent frameworks often hit a wall: too many tools, too much context in the prompt, and suddenly reliability tanks. This new paper, \"Attention Is All You Have,\" highlights a core issue where thousands of agent skills compete for a mere ~100 reliable trigger slots in an LLM's attention.\n\nThe problem is not the number of skills, but how they are exposed. Dumping every skill's description into the permanent system prompt causes dilution and a token tax on every message. The proposed solution is a novel skill protocol that decouples content, persistence, and auto-triggering.\n\nThis means agents only load skill descriptions when needed, using a path-based addressing system, dramatically reducing prompt space consumption. It is a critical shift for anyone building scalable, reliable AI agents, moving beyond naive prompt engineering to a more robust architectural pattern."
